Verified cycle-rewriting extension (2026-10-19)
==============================================
The additive Cycle_Checker session in thys/Cycle_Checker proves soundness of
ordinary self-embedding, cyclic power transport, and finite transport systems
with persistent strict progress. It defines cycle rewriting explicitly as
ordinary string rewriting modulo rotation, requiring a genuine rewrite in
every cycle step. A reversal bridge is proved as well.

tools/build_cycle_checker.py builds this session on a private clone of a
verified consolidated Proof_Checker heap and exports/compiles ceta-cycle.
It does not change existing production checkers or rebuild HOL/AFP. The source,
generated code, binary hashes and build logs are retained in the output tree.
The accepted front end is src/Haskell/Main_Cycle.hs. Its CycleTransport,
CycleEmbedding and CycleMorphism constructors are a native cycle-certificate
format, NOT ordinary SRS CPF or a claim of stock CPF schema support. Natural
number fields must be nonnegative. The generated executable checks each local
rule application, every transport equation, alphabet closure, and persistent
nonempty progress. Empty traces cannot establish nontermination by rotation.

Production build: target/cycle-production-20261019/ceta-cycle
SHA-256: ba7570bcdb56c1e2d6fa7b1f05251e6c07d5a36d8052a980af6c688496593961
The accompanying identity.json pins the exact exported source and warm parent.
Original-input correspondence and two independent checker invocations per
retained root remain mandatory campaign gates.


Files & Directories
===================
Following files are included in the distribution:

- COPYING: The GNU GPL license.
- COPYING.LESSER: The GNU LGPL license (based on the GPL).
- Makefile: GNU make build rules for CeTA.
- README: This file.
- generated: Contains all source files that have been automatically
  extracted from IsaFoR (for Haskell).
- src: Contains sources that are not automatically generated.
- examples: Contains example problems and proofs.
- xml: Contains all XML related files.


Compilation
===========
In order to compile CeTA you need: 

 * GHC (the Haskell compiler)

To build CeTA on your own, just type

  make 

This will create the binary 'ceta.' To test the binary on some proofs, use

  make test

To manually call ceta use something like

  ./ceta examples/div.proof.xml

If you want to generate the CeTA sources from the IsaFoR formalization, you
need mercurial (hg). Download the IsaFoR mercurial repository via

  hg clone -r v3.9 http://cl2-informatik.uibk.ac.at/rewriting/mercurial.cgi/IsaFoR

and follow the instructions in the accompanying README or README_devel file.


Dependencies
============
IsaFoR:   v3.9
Isabelle: Isabelle 2025-2
AFP:      Isabelle 2025-2 
